cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hcbic: How much data does it take to test an expert causal diagram?"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
# Add date-released and doi when the GitHub release is archived on Zenodo.
abstract: "An R package and analysis that asks how many observations are needed to recover, or to contradict, an expert-elicited causal diagram of an agroforestry and livelihoods system. It simulates data from the expert model, runs hill-climbing structure learning scored by the Bayesian information criterion, and reports recovery of the diagram and the power to detect each missing arc."
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata."
authors:
